   It also changes uv.lock:
     · s3fs 2026.4.0 → 2026.6.0

   Dependabot resolves for the oldest Python requires-python allows (3.10) and filters out releases that need a newer one: dnspython 2.9.2 needs Python >=3.11. It does not read [tool.uv] environments (python_full_version >= '3.12' and sys_platform == 'linux' and platform_machine == 'x86_64', python_full_version >= '3.12' and sys_platform == 'linux' and platform_machine == 'aarch64'), which lets uv lock these releases here.

   Verified with uv's resolver: 14 of 17 fixes resolve together.
   Then run: uv lock --upgrade-package anyio==4.14.2 --upgrade-package cryptography==50.0.0 --upgrade-package dnspython==2.9.2 --upgrade-package fsspec==2026.6.0 --upgrade-package gitpython==3.2.1 --upgrade-package hydra-core==1.3.6 --upgrade-package msgpack==1.2.3 --upgrade-package onnx==1.22.0 --upgrade-package pyasn1==0.6.5 --upgrade-package pydantic-settings==2.14.2 --upgrade-package pyjwt==2.15.0 --upgrade-package ray==2.56.0 --upgrade-package urllib3==2.8.0 --upgrade-package werkzeug==3.1.9
